  "id": "Compound::DB00946 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Phenprocoumon, through its structural similarities to Phenindione and Cyclobenzaprine, exhibits a shared mechanism of interaction with Cyp3a4, a key enzyme involved in drug metabolism. The evidence suggests that Phenprocoumon may act as a substrate or inhibitor of Cyp3a4, as it binds to the enzyme in some cases, particularly when it resembles Cyclobenzaprine. This binding is supported by the lowest common ancestor (LCA) relationships, which indicate that Phenprocoumon and its analogs share a common pathway to the organic molecule class, and thus may share a common mode of action with Cyp3a4. The presence of anticoagulant properties in these compounds further supports a direct interaction with Cyp3a4, as anticoagulants often target metabolic pathways involving cytochrome P450 enzymes. The integration of structural similarities and functional interactions across multiple paths suggests a plausible mechanistic link between Phenprocoumon and Cyp3a4, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
